# Class selectors `scripts/gates/dead-css.mjs` reports as unreferenced and that
# are not to be deleted. One `path<TAB>.selector` per line; a reason is
# required, because the only thing separating an accepted finding from an
# unfixed defect is what is written here.
#
# Empty, and that is the intended state. The matcher cannot see a class name
# assembled at runtime, so an entry here should name the expression that builds
# it. An entry that says "dead, but not mine to delete" is a deferral. Carry
# those in the change that owns the file.
#
# Some findings are never allow-listed. A custom property nothing reads, a
# `var()` nothing declares, a `var(--cco-*, fallback)`, a `--mdc-*` name and a
# deleted light-ramp hex are closed questions, so they fail unconditionally.
